{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/cell_status

    The Status cell of the notice table: a live/draft badge, plus a conflict badge when this
    notice competes with another repeating one for the same pages.

    Every background states its text colour. Bootstrap 4 gives .badge no colour at all and
    Bootstrap 5 defaults it to white, so the two branches fail on disjoint sets of fills;
    tests/local/bootstrap_compat_test.php enforces the pairing.

    The conflict badge explains itself twice: a title attribute for the pointer, and a
    visually-hidden sibling for assistive technology. An aria-label on a bare span has no role to
    attach to and is not announced reliably.

    Context variables required:
    * enabled (bool) — true for a live notice, false for a draft
    * hasclash (bool) — whether a conflict badge is shown
    * clashlabel (string) — the conflict badge text
    * clashexplanation (string) — which notices it competes with

    Example context (json):
    {
        "enabled": false,
        "hasclash": true,
        "clashlabel": "Conflict",
        "clashexplanation": "Competes with: Maintenance window"
    }
}}
<div class="local-awareness-statuscell">
    {{#enabled}}
        <span class="badge bg-success text-white">{{#str}}notice:status:live, local_awareness{{/str}}</span>
    {{/enabled}}
    {{^enabled}}
        <span class="badge bg-secondary text-dark">{{#str}}notice:status:draft, local_awareness{{/str}}</span>
    {{/enabled}}
    {{#hasclash}}
        <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark" title="{{clashexplanation}}">{{clashlabel}}<span
            class="visually-hidden"> — {{clashexplanation}}</span></span>
    {{/hasclash}}
</div>
